# Requisitions through the gateway, against the compose stack (docker compose up).
# Every password in the demo realm is "matchbook". Run the requests top to bottom.

@gateway = http://localhost:5300/api
@token = http://localhost:8080/realms/matchbook/protocol/openid-connect/token

# An active supplier's id, as Suppliers lists it at GET {{gateway}}/suppliers.
@supplierId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# A client-chosen id: sending the create twice with it returns the first requisition, not a second one.
@requisitionId = 0199b0f0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001

### Rita, a requester, signs in.
# @name rita
POST {{token}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=matchbook-cli&username=rita&password=matchbook

### Mark, the manager of ENG-PLATFORM, signs in.
# @name mark
POST {{token}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=matchbook-cli&username=mark&password=matchbook

### Fiona, a finance approver, signs in.
# @name fiona
POST {{token}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=matchbook-cli&username=fiona&password=matchbook

### Rita drafts a requisition of 12,500.00, over the finance threshold, under her own id.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{requisitionId}}",
  "costCentreCode": "ENG-PLATFORM",
  "supplierId": "{{supplierId}}",
  "justification": "Laptops for the two new platform engineers",
  "neededBy": "2027-06-30",
  "lines": [
    { "description": "Laptop", "quantity": 5, "unitOfMeasure": "EA", "unitPrice": 2400.00 },
    { "description": "Laptop bag", "quantity": 20, "unitOfMeasure": "EA", "unitPrice": 25.00 }
  ]
}

### Rita sends exactly the same create again, as a client would after a timeout: 201 with the same requisition.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{requisitionId}}",
  "costCentreCode": "ENG-PLATFORM",
  "supplierId": "{{supplierId}}",
  "justification": "Laptops for the two new platform engineers",
  "neededBy": "2027-06-30",
  "lines": [
    { "description": "Laptop", "quantity": 5, "unitOfMeasure": "EA", "unitPrice": 2400.00 },
    { "description": "Laptop bag", "quantity": 20, "unitOfMeasure": "EA", "unitPrice": 25.00 }
  ]
}

### Rita reads it back, with its lines, its (still empty) route and its timeline.
GET {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{requisitionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}

### Rita edits the draft, which only a draft allows; the id no longer repeats the create after this.
PUT {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{requisitionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "costCentreCode": "ENG-PLATFORM",
  "supplierId": "{{supplierId}}",
  "justification": "Laptops and docks for the two new platform engineers",
  "neededBy": "2027-06-30",
  "lines": [
    { "description": "Laptop", "quantity": 5, "unitOfMeasure": "EA", "unitPrice": 2400.00 },
    { "description": "Docking station", "quantity": 5, "unitOfMeasure": "EA", "unitPrice": 180.00 }
  ]
}

### Rita lists her requisitions, newest first; pass nextCursor back as after for the next page.
GET {{gateway}}/requisitions?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}

### Rita submits it; Budgets reserves the funds and the route is fixed a moment later.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{requisitionId}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}

### Rita cannot approve her own requisition: 403.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{requisitionId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}

### Mark's queue: what he can approve or reject right now.
GET {{gateway}}/approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{mark.response.body.access_token}}

### Fiona's queue is empty until Mark has signed the manager step.
GET {{gateway}}/approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{fiona.response.body.access_token}}

### Mark signs the manager step.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{requisitionId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{mark.response.body.access_token}}

### Mark cannot sign the finance step too: 403, even if he held the role.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{requisitionId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{mark.response.body.access_token}}

### Fiona signs the finance step, the last one: the requisition is approved and Purchasing drafts an order.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{requisitionId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{fiona.response.body.access_token}}

### The timeline now shows who did what, and when.
GET {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{requisitionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}

### Rita drafts a second, smaller requisition, this time letting the service choose the id.
# @name second
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "costCentreCode": "ENG-PLATFORM",
  "supplierId": "{{supplierId}}",
  "justification": "A standing desk",
  "neededBy": "2027-06-30",
  "lines": [ { "description": "Standing desk", "quantity": 1, "unitOfMeasure": "EA", "unitPrice": 640.00 } ]
}

### Rita submits the second one.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{second.response.body.id}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}

### Mark rejects it, with the reason the requester will read.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{second.response.body.id}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{mark.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "We have two unused standing desks on the third floor." }

### Rita drafts a third and withdraws it; a draft never reached Budgets, so nobody else hears of it.
# @name third
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "costCentreCode": "ENG-PLATFORM",
  "supplierId": "{{supplierId}}",
  "justification": "Spare keyboards",
  "neededBy": "2027-06-30",
  "lines": [ { "description": "Keyboard", "quantity": 10, "unitOfMeasure": "EA", "unitPrice": 45.00 } ]
}

### Rita cancels the third one.
POST {{gateway}}/requisitions/{{third.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{rita.response.body.access_token}}

### The service's OpenAPI document, through the gateway and without a token.
GET http://localhost:5300/openapi/requisitions.json
